###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The only energy-valued error is the harmonic Helmholtz free energy from phonons (Table S4); it is encoded as an energy MAE in meV/atom. Phonon-frequency MAEs (meV, Table S2) are vibrational energies rather than potential-energy errors and are not encoded.
# - Four checkpoints match registry models (MatterSim-v1.0.0-5M, SevenNet-0 11July2024, MACE-MP-0 2024-01-07-mace-128-L2, M3GNet-MP-2021.2.8-PES); the others are recorded as distributed checkpoints. SevenNet-MF-ompa applies NequIP by the registry convention.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/han2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

